<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Baptism is the sacrament of new birth in Christ: the gateway to Christian life, making us children of God, incorporating us into the Church, and imprinting an indelible character on the soul.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that Baptism is the &laquo;gateway to the sacraments&raquo; and necessary for salvation.</li>
<li>Discover the Old Testament prefigurations of Baptism (the Flood, the Red Sea).</li>
<li>Learn the matter, form, minister, and effects of the sacrament.</li>
<li>Understand how Baptism removes original sin and restores sanctifying grace.</li>
<li>Embrace the dignity of being a child of God and live from that identity.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Unless one is born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God&raquo; (Jn 3:5)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 1210-1284</p>

</section>

